# Env
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# bigcommerce.graphql and bigcommerce-graphql.d.ts are generated by
# `pnpm generate`, and are deliberately **committed** rather than ignored.
#
# They were ignored, on the theory that a generated file should be regenerated.
# Nothing regenerated them: `prebuild` runs only `build-config`, so a clean
# checkout had no schema and no gql.tada types, every `graphql()` document typed
# as `unknown`, and `next build` failed with 396 type errors. Locally it passed,
# because the files were sitting there untracked.
#
# Committing them is also the better design, for the same reason the font is
# vendored in app/fonts:
#
#   - a deploy needs no network and no BigCommerce credentials
#   - the types that were tested are the types that ship
#   - a schema change shows up in a diff and gets reviewed, instead of silently
#     changing types between two deploys of the same commit
#
# Run `pnpm generate` when the BigCommerce schema changes, and commit the result.

# Written by scripts/build-config.ts on prebuild. The committed file in
# lib/config/build-config.json is a placeholder so a fresh clone typechecks;
# real values are written at build time.
!lib/config/build-config.json

# Tooling
.eslintcache
